    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Dear Listener,\n\tWhat you are about to hear is a compilation of many, many hours of work.  It is one attempt at rendering the words and thoughts of many people into a fun and easy-to-listen-to format.  By no means is this a professional work or the finale to the story—at some point one must decide to let go.  The work can always be altered, improved, revised, restructured, criticized, etc. and deadlines help to force a creator to “call it quits,” at least for now.\n\tThis podcast is an informal exploration of nudity and its role and place on the campus of Stanford University.  It includes interviews and recordings of the following: current undergraduate students of all grade levels, Frosh Resident Fellows, a dean of undergraduate student life, a prospective freshman, student residents of a cooperative house (Synergy), an official Stanford Admissions information session, and people unfamiliar with Stanford’s campus culture.\nEnjoy,\nL",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
